YAAP - schoolmann - sam hum law mal - wishless genoless polyselfless

Ascended my seventh role. This was my first serious game on a remote
server (nethack.alt.org). I think the connection lag helped my
play--kept me from typing too fast. I proved to myself that I *can* play
in ascii, even though I've always preferred tiles before, and I can play
in a console, even though "--more--" drives me nuts. I didn't start the
game in a "conduct or die" mode, for those who rate conducts that way,
but I'm happy to have made wishless for the first time. Genoless was
accidental; I never found a scroll of genocide the whole game, and since
I was going wishless, I didn't have the option to wish for one.

Incidentally, my character's name is "schoolmann" simply because that's
the handle that I logged into n.a.o with (before finding out that that
would necessarily be the character's name). On my own system, I'd have
played him as "Ibanez."

Adventure:

Fell through traps very early on to levels two and three; worked my way
back up to rejoin my pet on dlvl 1 while remaining at Xp:1:11. Got some
useful stuff including magic whistle, BoH, and magic marker in a large
tool shop on level 5. Did Sokoban before Mines and got AoR--lucky,
because I'd already found a bag that turned out to be a BoH. Found early
cloak of displacement and used it down to the Valley.

Levelport trap dropped me two levels in Mines; almost got killed getting
back up to where my pet was. Minetown had a coaligned temple; did some
saccing and got Snickersnee. Found a luckstone before hitting Mine's
End, so I didn't mess around in the lower levels of the mines any longer
than necessary.

While in the Mines, I tamed two cats and then polytrapped them into an
Elf lord and a grey dragon. I named them Rosencrantz and Guildenstern
respectively, which worked out fine until Guildenstern got hungry and
killed and ate Rosencrantz. Oh well. Rode Guildenstern for a while,
until he attacked a cockatrice and stoned himself.

Dlvl 12 was a bones level. My first indication of this was having
Schroedinger's Cat just wander up to me (without me even having seen a
QM). Turns out it was left by a character named fizban (now a human
mummy). Fizban had set up a stash around an altar, and I got a +2 GDSM
and 9 potions of holy water from the stash. Thanks, fizban! Turned out
that was the only bones level I hit during the game.

Cleared the Castle and found the Castle Wand of Wishing. By this time, I
had two extra magic lamps (besides a light source) and several smoky
potions (don't recall what they were; something easy to get and
unharmful to drink). I already had GDSM, though, and decided to go
wishless if I could get away with it. The main thing I didn't have was
speed boots.

Still wearing CoD, got level drained too many times by vampires in the
Valley; always leveled back up again, but decided to switch to a robe,
and work up some spells. Used magic missile to good effect, also
practiced clerical spells by casting protection repeatedly.

After clearing Castle, went back to do the Quest. Speed boots found on
third level of quest. Decided to do some sacfesting to try for a better
weapon, but just kept getting foobanes and foosmashers. Took a long time
to get ?oEA. Used up two magic markers I'd found enchanting up armor and
weapons as much as I could. At this point, my AC was-32, -37 when
casting protection. I would like to have gotten better AC and enchanted
my weapons better, but didn't want to break wishless conduct in order to
do it.

I ended up laboriously mapping out most of Gehennom on foot, looking for
magic markers (never found any more), since I didn't have the magic
mapping spell or (until much later) detect treasure. Fell through a trap
door around dlvl 33 or 34, and went down to 36. Working my way back up,
found that 35 was Baalzebub. Much much later, after making it down to
the VS level, found out that Baalzebub's level was the stairs to Vlad's.

After mapping out the whole dungeon, I went back up to dlvl 13 and 14 to
do more saccing. I really wanted to get Greyswandir or at least a
*brand, but I never did. I also did some praying, and got one extra
point of protection (naked AC 0), a couple of golden glows, and some
spellbooks. While sacfesting, I created a MMF right next to me, who
proceeded immediately to brainsuck me; as luck would have it, most of
the levels I forgot were Gehennom levels, so I had to go through mapping
parts of it all over again. Aarrgghh! At least this time I had no need
to map out the rest of a level once I'd found the stairs, and I'd
knocked out some holes in the walls which helped lead me to the stairs
sometimes. I also had four scrolls of magic mapping which luckily I'd
saved for just such an emergency.

By the time I was ready to go for the Amulet, I'd amassed (or poly'd)
about five wands of death. I used cone of cold on the moats (at skilled,
so the targetted version); it was cool to trap eels in ice. I WoD'd
Rodney, levelported down to the VS level, tele'd over to the VS, did the
invocation, went downstairs and then up, and then used the levelport
trick to get down to the Sanctum level, arriving in the lower left
corner of the level. Got into the Sanctum itself, grabbed the Amulet,
and quaffed a cursed potion of gain level to get out of there. Never
even saw the graveyard part. Gotta love it.

Got mysterious forced *a lot*. I have more patience with this than most
people do, but it was really beginning to irritate me. Ended up using a
lot of scrolls of teleport and my three other potions of gain level, and
still had to walk through a lot of levels. Thank the devteam for the
travel command; I would have gone nuts without it. Luckily, most of the
mysterious forcing was over by the time I got up to Juiblex, so I didn't
have to traverse that more than once (actually, I think I used a c!oGL
on that one, so I never had to traverse it at all on the way up).

Rodney appeared several times on the way up; I kept on using my wands of
death on him; they missed surprisingly often, but I never ran out of
charges. The one time when playing ascii really messed with my game was
on Earth, when the Elf Lord moved next to me, I thought Rodney had
double-troubled me. I ended up taking out the Elf Lord before Rodney.

I had alchemized more HP than I've ever done with a character before
(more than 350) so I wasn't too worried about the Planes. Unfortunately,
I had only gotten two scrolls of gold detection, so I had to use them
sparingly (Earth and Water). I thought I could use a wand of SDD to find
the portals on Air and Fire, but it turned out that it had a limited
range. I got engulfed by Air Elementals several times, but had enough hp
and spare !oFH to deal with them without any worries. The stupidest
thing I did on the planes was to switch to boots of water walking on
Fire (at +0 enchantment) and then forget ever to switch back to my +4
speed boots. Duh! On Water I dove out of my bubble a couple of times,
wrongly thinking that water walking boots would let me do that; I ended
up diluting some potions and blanking some scrolls, none of which
mattered in the end.

On Astral, the right section was guarded by Pestilence, so I headed
toward the center one. Death took my max hp down to 377 from the 390s.
I'm surprised I managed to get to the altar as easily as I did without
speed boots (or jumping; I've done it with jumping boots before). I
think this is my first ascension in which the first altar I hit was the
right one. I'm still too much of a chicken to mess around once I've
found it (although I was planning on using confused ?oTaming to make
lots of pets, which never happened) so I just #offered the Amulet and
went to my reward.

Managed wishless, genoless, and polyselfless in less than 62,000 turns.
I actually found rings of poly and poly control relatively early on, but
I didn't really know what else I'd like to poly into (I'm too paranoid
about footrices to poly into a vampire lord, for example), so I just
didn't. Some of my own personal challenges were no Elbereth and no
credit cloning. I probably could have ascended in less than 50,000 turns
if I hadn't spent a bunch of time saccing (mostly wasted) and mapping
and remapping Gehennom; and I wasn't particularly going for a speed
ascension.

